ues are not guaranteed to be unique. If the "},{"code":"URLComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has an empty query component, returns an empty array. If the "},{"code":"URLComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has no query component, returns nil."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The setter combines an array containing any number of "},{"code":"URLQueryItem","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, each of which represents a single key-value pair, into a query string and sets the "},{"code":"URLComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" query property. Passing an empty array sets the query component of the "},{"code":"URLComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to an empty string. Passing nil removes the query component of the "},{"code":"URLComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If a name-value pair in a query is empty (i.e. the query string starts with ‘&’, ends with ‘&’, or has “&&” within it), you get a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLQueryItem"},{"type":"text","text":" with a zero-length name and a nil value. If a query’s name-value pair has nothing before the equals sign, you get a zero-length name. If a query’s name-value pair has nothing after the equals sign, you get a zero-length value. If a query’s name-value pair has no equals sign, the query name-value pair string is the name and you get a nil value."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"queryItems","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"URLQueryItem","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials12URLQueryItemV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"nam